- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycles): 5 unchecked items focused on storage-
  agnostic vocabulary drift. Most subsumed by the brevity rewrite if the
  rewrite excises retired regressions entirely.

## Retro

provisionBrain is the pattern-canonical example of a spec that grew because
every retired regression earned its own outcome and every retired identifier
earned its own Bad example. The Brevity Contract's outcomes-purpose test is
explicit: "if a unit test could catch this violation, it does not belong in
outcomes." Every retired-step-builder rejection, every retired-`brainPath`
parameter check, every retired-arg-index-introspection rule is unit-testable.

The spec should commit to "provisionBrain plans exactly two InitStep records
— scaffold the bundled template, plan the MCP entry — and writes nothing to
disk" and let the negative-rule enforcement live in code with focused unit
tests. The retired-name enumeration is git history.
